(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "kotoba-lang/dtn の static multi-hop relay（:routes / :relay action / hop-count）の設計根拠" "transport 層の宛先不一致 inbox バグの修正根拠")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "adr-2607161922-kotoba-lang-dtn-multi-hop-relay-routing"), (:adr/doc_type :adr), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-16"), (:adr/body "---\nid: adr-2607161922-kotoba-lang-dtn-multi-hop-relay-routing\ntitle: \"ADR-2607161922: kotoba-lang/dtn gains static multi-hop relay routing (route-decision :relay) and fixes a destination-mismatch inbox bug\"\nstatus: accepted\ndoc_type: adr\ntopic: telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite\nauthoritative: true\nlast_verified: 2026-07-16\nauthoritative_for:\n  - kotoba-lang/dtn の static multi-hop relay（:routes / :relay action / hop-count）の設計根拠\n  - transport 層の宛先不一致 inbox バグの修正根拠\nrelated:\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity.edn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn\nsupersedes: []\nsuperseded_by: []\n---\n\n# ADR-2607161922: kotoba-lang/dtn gains static multi-hop relay routing (route-decision :relay) and fixes a destination-mismatch inbox bug\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter ADR-2607161852 closed the durability and integrity gaps, `kotoba.dtn.router/route-decision`\nstill had only two outcomes: forward if the destination is a *directly*\nreachable neighbor, or store. There was no way for a message to travel\nthrough an intermediate node when no direct link to the final destination\nexisted — which is a real limitation on what a delay-tolerant *network* is\nfor (vs. point-to-point messaging with retry), and the next-highest-value\nitem from the gap inventory given when asked *「残りのgapは?」*.\n\nAuditing the existing transport for this change surfaced a related latent\ncorrectness bug: `kotoba.dtn.transport.tcp`'s inbound handler accepted any\nsuccessfully-decoded (and, if configured, signature-verified) bundle\nstraight into its own `:inbox`, without checking whether the bundle's\n`:dtn/destination` actually matched the receiving node's own EID. That was\nharmless while every message happened to be sent directly to its intended\nrecipient (the only pattern possible before this ADR), but would have been\nsilently wrong the moment relaying existed: a relay node would have\nabsorbed messages addressed to someone else as if they were its own.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Decision 1: `route-decision` gains an optional `:relay` action, not a rewrite of the existing two\n\n`kotoba.dtn.router/route-decision`'s existing signature, direct-neighbor\nbehavior, and store-fallback behavior are all unchanged — every prior\ncaller and test keeps passing unmodified. New optional kwargs `:routes`\n(a coll of `{:dtn/destination eid :dtn/next-hop eid}` entries — a\ncaller-supplied, statically-configured routing table), `:hop-count`\n(default 0), and `:max-hops` (default 8) enable a third outcome: when no\ndirect link to the destination is reachable, but a `:routes` entry names a\nnext-hop that IS reachable and `:hop-count < :max-hops`, return\n`{:dtn/action :relay :dtn/via <link> :dtn/next-hop <eid>}` — a result kept\nstructurally distinct from `:forward` (same wire action, different meaning:\n\"this bundle isn't for whoever I hand it to next, it's a hop toward\nsomeone else\"). Missing route, unreachable next-hop, or hop-count at/over\nthe cap all fall through to `:store`, exactly as the no-relay path already\ndid — a bundle that has hopped too many times without arriving gets held,\nnot endlessly bounced. This is deliberately **static/pre-configured\nsingle-hop relay**, not automatic route discovery, topology advertisement,\nor full Contact Graph Routing (RFC 9174) — one step beyond the prior\n\"direct-neighbor-or-store\" heuristic, named as exactly that in the\nnamespace docstring, not oversold as general multi-hop routing.\n\n### Decision 2: fix the destination-mismatch bug as part of this change, not separately\n\n`kotoba.dtn.transport.tcp`'s inbound handler now checks\n`(:dtn/destination bundle)` against the receiving node's own EID\nimmediately after (any configured) signature verification. A match keeps\nthe exact prior behavior (decode, add to `:inbox`, log `DTN-RECV`). A\nmismatch is treated as a relay request: hop-count is incremented, a\ndistinct `DTN-RELAY` line is logged, and the bundle is re-submitted through\nthe same `route-and-send!` path a locally-originated send would use — using\nthe relay node's OWN `:links`/`:routes`, so it may forward further or store\nif it, too, lacks a path. A relayed-through bundle is never added to the\nrelaying node's own `:inbox`. A lightweight per-node `:seen-bundle-ids` set\nsuppresses exact-duplicate re-relays of the same bundle id, a minimal,\nhonest loop-prevention addition alongside the hop-count cap — not a claim\nof full duplicate-bundle detection across restarts or nodes.\n\n### Decision 3: verify the relay is real, not merely a returned value\n\nDemo scenario 6 configures node A with **no** peer/link entry for node C\nat all — only for node B, plus a `:routes` entry naming C reachable via B —\nand node B with a genuine direct link to C. A sends to C over real TCP.\nAssertions check three things, not just \"did C receive it\": C's `:inbox`\nactually contains the message; B's `:inbox` does **NOT** contain it\n(proving the Decision 2 fix — B correctly relayed instead of absorbing);\nand B's own log shows it made a real `DTN-RELAY` routing decision (not an\nout-of-band shortcut in the test harness). All five prior scenarios (1\nthrough 4b) were re-run unmodified and still pass.\n\nAs with the two prior follow-up ADRs, this was independently re-verified\nby the orchestrating session from a cold clone before writing this ADR's\nVerification section, not trusted from the implementing agent's report\nalone.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test` → 27 tests / 126 assertions (was 112; +14 new: 8 router relay/hop-count/max-hops cases plus supporting coverage), 0 failures, 0 errors. Independently re-run from a cold clone.\n- `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings. Independently re-run.\n- `nbb --classpath \"src:test:../phone/src:../html/src:../css/src\" test/kotoba/dtn/transport/tcp_demo.cljs` → `RESULT: 6/6 scenarios passed`, exit 0 (scenarios 1-4b from the prior two ADRs unmodified and still passing; new scenario 5/6 — A→B→C relay — passes, with B's own `DTN-RELAY` log line and B's untouched `:inbox` both confirmed). Independently re-run from a cold clone, output matches the implementing agent's report.\n- Pushed to `github.com/kotoba-lang/dtn` (public), commit `54fe04c34eaa5c92f561956ec7e64fd33ce89301`.\n- `manifest/west.yml`: pin advanced via `--entry dtn` (1-line diff, `a89edf50cfcc→54fe04c34eaa`, `verify-west-pins: 1 件の pin 変更をすべて検証 OK` — 3 unrelated pending pin changes elsewhere in the tree were correctly left untouched by the `--only dtn` scoping), landed via an isolated sibling-path worktree + GitHub API server-side merge, matching all three prior ADRs' landing procedure.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/dtn` can now deliver a message through one statically\n  configured intermediate relay when no direct link to the final\n  destination exists — a genuine step from \"point-to-point messaging with\n  retry\" toward \"a network,\" which is what the whole design exists to be.\n- The destination-mismatch fix (Decision 2) closes a latent correctness\n  bug that existed since ADR-2607161817's original transport, even though\n  it never manifested under that ADR's only-ever-direct-send usage pattern\n  — worth recording plainly as a bug found and fixed while adding a\n  feature, not just a new capability.\n- Relay routing is single-hop only (A relays via B to reach C; A relaying\n  via B via D to reach C — i.e. more than one intermediate hop — is not\n  tested and not claimed, though `route-decision`'s recursive-feeling\n  structure at the transport layer, where each relaying node re-runs its\n  own `route-and-send!`, suggests it may already work for longer chains;\n  this ADR only verifies and claims the two-hop case actually demonstrated\n  in scenario 6).\n- Still explicitly undone, unchanged from the prior two ADRs' inventories:\n  automatic route discovery/advertisement (`kotoba-lang/net` gossip\n  composition), NAT traversal (`kotoba-lang/turn` composition), PKI/replay\n  protection, remaining RFC 9171 wire-format details, mesh-radio/satellite\n  hardware, real carrier gateway credentials, a consuming cloud-itonami\n  actor.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **Dynamic route discovery/advertisement** (nodes announce reachability to\n  each other, building routing tables automatically). Rejected for this\n  ADR: materially larger scope, edges into `kotoba-lang/net`'s gossip\n  domain already named as deferred composition work, and risks reproducing\n  the \"honestly-scoped heuristic vs. full CGR\" line this repo has drawn\n  since ADR-2607161743 — static/configured routes keep the claim exactly\n  matched to what was built and verified.\n- **Per-node visited-node-list loop prevention** (each bundle carries the\n  list of nodes it's already passed through) instead of a simple hop-count\n  cap. Rejected as more machinery than this pass's honest scope needs; a\n  hop-count cap plus a duplicate-bundle-id suppression set catches the\n  practical failure modes (misconfigured route cycles, redundant re-relay)\n  without adding a growing per-bundle field.\n- **Deferring the destination-mismatch fix to a separate ADR/PR.**\n  Rejected: the bug was inert before relay routing existed and only\n  becomes a real hazard once relaying is added, so fixing it in the same\n  change that introduces the hazard is the coherent unit of work — not a\n  scope-creep addition.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity.edn`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/README.edn` — https://github.com/kotoba-lang/dtn\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/src/kotoba/dtn/router.cljc`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/src/kotoba/dtn/transport/tcp.cljs`\n"), (:adr/artifacts "{:kotoba-lang-dtn \"kotoba-lang/dtn @ 54fe04c34eaa (pushed, public)\", :manifest \"orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn pin advanced via --entry dtn, pin-verified\"}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607161922: kotoba-lang/dtn gains static multi-hop relay routing (route-decision :relay) and fixes a destination-mismatch inbox bug"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))